 "notes": "95% C.L. black-hole superradiance exclusion contours traced from the vector paths of Fig. 2 (example exclusion functions for two typical BHs). The paper's exclusion plane is (m_a, f_pert) with f_pert^2 = m^2/lambda the perturbative axion decay constant; reported coupling is 1/f_pert in GeV^-1, with the region excluded for couplings BELOW the curve (f_pert above the boundary, where self-interactions are too weak to quench superradiance via Bosenova). Two disjoint mass islands concatenated in mass order: SMBH NGC 7469 (m ~ 6.4e-19 to 1.6e-18 eV, boundary reaching f_pert ~ 6.8e14 GeV) and stellar-mass GRO J1655-40 (m ~ 2.4e-13 to 1.3e-11 eV, reaching f_pert ~ 2.5e12 GeV). Contour endpoints at 1/f_a ~ 4e-19 GeV^-1 are where the contours meet the plot's upper axis (f_pert ~ 2.5e18 GeV); the exclusion extends to arbitrarily weak self-interaction (smaller 1/f_a) within each mass window. Limit is independent of the local dark-matter density. The paper's headline Fig. 3 (fraction of excluded Calabi-Yau manifolds vs Hodge number) is a landscape statistic, not a coupling limit; Fig. 2 contains the paper's exclusion in the canonical (mass, 1/f_a) plane.",
